{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 0, "result": {"protocolVersion": "2025-06-18", "capabilities": {"tools": {"listChanged": false}, "resources": {}, "prompts": {}}, "serverInfo": {"name": "ucas", "title": "ucas, a computer algebra system for programmers", "version": "1"}, "instructions": "ucas analyses functions (exhaustively on machine types), does exact algebra and calculus, transforms, number theory and finite fields, and finds cheaper implementations, each answer checked or proved.  Expressions are ucas syntax strings; give parameters types (x: u8, x: f32, x: real) where it matters.  Definitions persist across calls.  An ambiguous input is an error listing its readings: retry with args.assume.KEY.  structuredContent holds the typed result, checks and proof."}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 1, "result": {}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 2, "result": {"tools": [{"name": "analyze", "title": "Analyse a function", "description": "Exhaustive or sampled analysis of a function over its domain (machine types u8..u64, i8..i64, f32, f64, real, int): values, range, where it is defined, wrapping and C UB, critical points, equivalence of two functions (with a counterexample), error and fit of an approximation, cost under a GPU cost model, minimal gate networks (with a proof of minimality), cheaper equivalent implementations, polynomial/rational approximations.\n\nCall with {\"op\": OP, \"args\": {...}}; expressions are ucas syntax strings (x^2 sin(x), isqrt(x: u4)) or an AST ({\"op\": \"+\", \"args\": [...]}).  Ops (* = required arg):\n- show(f*): the function, typed\n- table(f*, max): values at the points of the domain\n- parse(expr*): the expression fully parenthesised\n- range(f*, nocrit): min/max over the domain\n- domain(f*): the conditions of the partial operations and the inputs where F is defined\n- wrap(f*): nuw/nsw per operation, C UB, end-to-end agreement with the mathematical result\n- crit(f*): critical points, extrema, inflection points\n- equiv(f*, g*): equal on F's domain? (with a counterexample)\n- fit(g*, f*, metric): choose G's extra parameters to approximate F\n- error(g*, f*): error of G as an approximation of F\n- cost(f*, model): price under a cost model\n- gates(f*, basis, max, nodes, as_c): minimal gate network, with proof\n- find(f*, n, max): cheaper implementations under the cost model\n- more(n): the next results of the last find\n- approx(f*, in, options): polynomial/rational approximations, measured\n- approx_more(n): more candidates of the last approx\nEvery op also takes assume (answers to ambiguities, from an error's readings), defaults, timeout_s, files.  Example: {\"op\": \"show\", \"args\": {\"f\": \"x^3 - 3x\"}}", "inputSchema": {"type": "object", "properties": {"op": {"type": "string", "enum": ["show", "table", "parse", "range", "domain", "wrap", "crit", "equiv", "fit", "error", "cost", "gates", "find", "more", "approx", "approx_more"], "description": "the operation"}, "args": {"type": "object", "description": "the op's named arguments (see the description; the exact schema of each op is in the session tool's schema op)"}}, "required": ["op"], "additionalProperties": false}, "outputSchema": {"type": "object", "required": ["id", "ok", "cmd"], "properties": {"id": {"description": "the request's id, as given (null if none)"}, "ok": {"type": "boolean"}, "cmd": {"type": ["string", "null"]}, "ucas": {"description": "the ucas statements that ran (error positions refer to them)", "type": "string"}, "structured": {"description": "result has fields beyond text", "type": "boolean"}, "result": {"description": "the command's fields (kind, ...); exact values as {value, exact}; expressions as ucas strings that parse back; unstructured commands give {text}", "type": "object"}, "results": {"description": "every result, when the request ran several commands", "type": "array"}, "notes": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"kind": {"enum": ["rule", "info", "assumed", "default"]}, "text": {"type": "string"}}}}, "conditions": {"description": "where the answer holds", "type": "array", "items": {"type": "string"}}, "checks": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"kind": {"type": "string"}, "points": {"type": "integer"}, "max_diff": {"type": "number"}, "passed": {"type": "boolean"}, "text": {"type": "string"}}}}, "proof": {"type": "object", "properties": {"kind": {"enum": ["symbolic", "exhaustive", "sat", "numeric", "search"]}, "text": {"type": "string"}}}, "files": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"name": {"type": "string"}, "mime": {"type": "string"}, "bytes": {"type": "integer"}, "path": {"type": "string"}, "base64": {"type": "string"}}}}, "text": {"description": "the output as the CLI prints it", "type": "string"}, "error": {"type": "object", "required": ["code", "message"], "properties": {"code": {"enum": ["bad_json", "bad_request", "unknown_command", "parse_error", "domain_error", "unsupported", "failed", "ambiguous", "needs_input", "not_understood", "timeout", "internal"]}, "message": {"type": "string"}, "pos": {"type": "object", "properties": {"line": {"type": "integer"}, "col": {"type": "integer"}}}, "key": {"description": "ambiguous: the args.assume key that picks a reading", "type": "string"}, "readings": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"index": {"type": "integer"}, "reading": {"type": "string"}, "default": {"type": "boolean"}, "how": {"type": "string"}}}}, "how": {"type": "string"}}}}}}, {"name": "calculus", "title": "Calculus", "description": "Derivatives (higher, partial, mixed), gradient, Hessian, Laplacian, Jacobian, Wronskian, limits (symbolic and numeric), Taylor series, implicit derivatives, integrals (antiderivative checked by differentiating back; definite also numerically; contour integrals with around), closed forms of sums and loops, evaluation schemes, ODEs.\n\nCall with {\"op\": OP, \"args\": {...}}; expressions are ucas syntax strings (x^2 sin(x), isqrt(x: u4)) or an AST ({\"op\": \"+\", \"args\": [...]}).  Ops (* = required arg):\n- diff(f*, vars, order): derivative (higher, partial, mixed)\n- grad(f*, at): the gradient\n- hessian(f*, at): the Hessian (and at a point the second-derivative test)\n- laplacian(f*, at): the Laplacian\n- jacobian(fs*, wrt, at): the Jacobian matrix\n- wronskian(fs*, var): the Wronskian and linear independence\n- limit(f*, var, to*, side): a limit, symbolically and numerically\n- taylor(f*, var, at, order): Taylor polynomial, checked\n- implicit(equation*, for, wrt, order): dy/dx of an implicit curve\n- integrate(f*, var, from, to, around): antiderivative (checked by differentiating back) or definite integral\n- antiderivative(f*, var): an antiderivative + C\n- closed(f*): closed forms of sums, products, loops\n- scheme(f*, model): evaluation schemes priced\n- continuous(f*): sums as integrals, loops as ODEs\n- dsolve(name*, from, to, steps): solve a defined ODE (symbolic or numeric)\nEvery op also takes assume (answers to ambiguities, from an error's readings), defaults, timeout_s, files.  Example: {\"op\": \"diff\", \"args\": {\"f\": \"x^3 - 3x\"}}", "inputSchema": {"type": "object", "properties": {"op": {"type": "string", "enum": ["diff", "grad", "hessian", "laplacian", "jacobian", "wronskian", "limit", "taylor", "implicit", "integrate", "antiderivative", "closed", "scheme", "continuous", "dsolve"], "description": "the operation"}, "args": {"type": "object", "description": "the op's named arguments (see the description; the exact schema of each op is in the session tool's schema op)"}}, "required": ["op"], "additionalProperties": false}, "outputSchema": {"type": "object", "required": ["id", "ok", "cmd"], "properties": {"id": {"description": "the request's id, as given (null if none)"}, "ok": {"type": "boolean"}, "cmd": {"type": ["string", "null"]}, "ucas": {"description": "the ucas statements that ran (error positions refer to them)", "type": "string"}, "structured": {"description": "result has fields beyond text", "type": "boolean"}, "result": {"description": "the command's fields (kind, ...); exact values as {value, exact}; expressions as ucas strings that parse back; unstructured commands give {text}", "type": "object"}, "results": {"description": "every result, when the request ran several commands", "type": "array"}, "notes": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"kind": {"enum": ["rule", "info", "assumed", "default"]}, "text": {"type": "string"}}}}, "conditions": {"description": "where the answer holds", "type": "array", "items": {"type": "string"}}, "checks": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"kind": {"type": "string"}, "points": {"type": "integer"}, "max_diff": {"type": "number"}, "passed": {"type": "boolean"}, "text": {"type": "string"}}}}, "proof": {"type": "object", "properties": {"kind": {"enum": ["symbolic", "exhaustive", "sat", "numeric", "search"]}, "text": {"type": "string"}}}, "files": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"name": {"type": "string"}, "mime": {"type": "string"}, "bytes": {"type": "integer"}, "path": {"type": "string"}, "base64": {"type": "string"}}}}, "text": {"description": "the output as the CLI prints it", "type": "string"}, "error": {"type": "object", "required": ["code", "message"], "properties": {"code": {"enum": ["bad_json", "bad_request", "unknown_command", "parse_error", "domain_error", "unsupported", "failed", "ambiguous", "needs_input", "not_understood", "timeout", "internal"]}, "message": {"type": "string"}, "pos": {"type": "object", "properties": {"line": {"type": "integer"}, "col": {"type": "integer"}}}, "key": {"description": "ambiguous: the args.assume key that picks a reading", "type": "string"}, "readings": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"index": {"type": "integer"}, "reading": {"type": "string"}, "default": {"type": "boolean"}, "how": {"type": "string"}}}}, "how": {"type": "string"}}}}}}, {"name": "algebra", "title": "Symbolic algebra", "description": "Polynomials and rational functions over Q, exactly: expand, factor, simplify (conditions where a factor cancelled), partial fractions, gcd/lcm, resultants, discriminants, division, solving equations and systems (every solution substituted back), substitution.\n\nCall with {\"op\": OP, \"args\": {...}}; expressions are ucas syntax strings (x^2 sin(x), isqrt(x: u4)) or an AST ({\"op\": \"+\", \"args\": [...]}).  Ops (* = required arg):\n- expand(f*): expanded over Q\n- factor(f*): factored over Q\n- simplify(f*): the simplest normal form\n- together(f*): one fraction\n- cancel(f*): common factors cancelled\n- collect(f*, var): collected in a variable\n- apart(f*, var): partial fractions\n- gcd(p*, q*): polynomial gcd\n- lcm(p*, q*): polynomial lcm\n- resultant(p*, q*, var): the resultant\n- discriminant(p*, var): the discriminant\n- quo(p*, q*, var): polynomial quotient\n- rem(p*, q*, var): polynomial remainder\n- divide(p*, q*, var): division with remainder\n- solve(equations*, for): equations and systems, every solution substituted back\n- substitute(values*, f*): F at values\nEvery op also takes assume (answers to ambiguities, from an error's readings), defaults, timeout_s, files.  Example: {\"op\": \"expand\", \"args\": {\"f\": \"x^3 - 3x\"}}", "inputSchema": {"type": "object", "properties": {"op": {"type": "string", "enum": ["expand", "factor", "simplify", "together", "cancel", "collect", "apart", "gcd", "lcm", "resultant", "discriminant", "quo", "rem", "divide", "solve", "substitute"], "description": "the operation"}, "args": {"type": "object", "description": "the op's named arguments (see the description; the exact schema of each op is in the session tool's schema op)"}}, "required": ["op"], "additionalProperties": false}, "outputSchema": {"type": "object", "required": ["id", "ok", "cmd"], "properties": {"id": {"description": "the request's id, as given (null if none)"}, "ok": {"type": "boolean"}, "cmd": {"type": ["string", "null"]}, "ucas": {"description": "the ucas statements that ran (error positions refer to them)", "type": "string"}, "structured": {"description": "result has fields beyond text", "type": "boolean"}, "result": {"description": "the command's fields (kind, ...); exact values as {value, exact}; expressions as ucas strings that parse back; unstructured commands give {text}", "type": "object"}, "results": {"description": "every result, when the request ran several commands", "type": "array"}, "notes": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"kind": {"enum": ["rule", "info", "assumed", "default"]}, "text": {"type": "string"}}}}, "conditions": {"description": "where the answer holds", "type": "array", "items": {"type": "string"}}, "checks": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"kind": {"type": "string"}, "points": {"type": "integer"}, "max_diff": {"type": "number"}, "passed": {"type": "boolean"}, "text": {"type": "string"}}}}, "proof": {"type": "object", "properties": {"kind": {"enum": ["symbolic", "exhaustive", "sat", "numeric", "search"]}, "text": {"type": "string"}}}, "files": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"name": {"type": "string"}, "mime": {"type": "string"}, "bytes": {"type": "integer"}, "path": {"type": "string"}, "base64": {"type": "string"}}}}, "text": {"description": "the output as the CLI prints it", "type": "string"}, "error": {"type": "object", "required": ["code", "message"], "properties": {"code": {"enum": ["bad_json", "bad_request", "unknown_command", "parse_error", "domain_error", "unsupported", "failed", "ambiguous", "needs_input", "not_understood", "timeout", "internal"]}, "message": {"type": "string"}, "pos": {"type": "object", "properties": {"line": {"type": "integer"}, "col": {"type": "integer"}}}, "key": {"description": "ambiguous: the args.assume key that picks a reading", "type": "string"}, "readings": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"index": {"type": "integer"}, "reading": {"type": "string"}, "default": {"type": "boolean"}, "how": {"type": "string"}}}}, "how": {"type": "string"}}}}}}, {"name": "properties", "title": "Properties of a function", "description": "Monotonicity, period, classification (identify: polynomials, conics, ODEs ...), zeros, parity, symmetry, bounds, injective/surjective/bijective, continuity, convexity, asymptotes; each tagged proved, exhaustive or numeric.\n\nCall with {\"op\": OP, \"args\": {...}}; expressions are ucas syntax strings (x^2 sin(x), isqrt(x: u4)) or an AST ({\"op\": \"+\", \"args\": [...]}).  Ops (* = required arg):\n- monotonic(f*, var, in): increasing/decreasing, intervals\n- period(f*, var): the fundamental period\n- identify(f*): classify an expression, equation, conic or ODE\n- zeros(f*): the zeros (exact for polynomials)\n- parity(f*): even/odd, symmetries\n- symmetry(f*): axes x = c, centres, f(x, y) = f(y, x)\n- bounded(f*): bounds, poles, growth\n- injective(f*): one to one? (with a witness)\n- surjective(f*, onto): onto? (with a value never taken)\n- bijective(f*): a bijection?\n- continuity(f*): discontinuities by kind\n- convexity(f*): convex/concave intervals\n- asymptotes(f*): vertical, horizontal, oblique\nEvery op also takes assume (answers to ambiguities, from an error's readings), defaults, timeout_s, files.  Example: {\"op\": \"monotonic\", \"args\": {\"f\": \"x^3 - 3x\"}}", "inputSchema": {"type": "object", "properties": {"op": {"type": "string", "enum": ["monotonic", "period", "identify", "zeros", "parity", "symmetry", "bounded", "injective", "surjective", "bijective", "continuity", "convexity", "asymptotes"], "description": "the operation"}, "args": {"type": "object", "description": "the op's named arguments (see the description; the exact schema of each op is in the session tool's schema op)"}}, "required": ["op"], "additionalProperties": false}, "outputSchema": {"type": "object", "required": ["id", "ok", "cmd"], "properties": {"id": {"description": "the request's id, as given (null if none)"}, "ok": {"type": "boolean"}, "cmd": {"type": ["string", "null"]}, "ucas": {"description": "the ucas statements that ran (error positions refer to them)", "type": "string"}, "structured": {"description": "result has fields beyond text", "type": "boolean"}, "result": {"description": "the command's fields (kind, ...); exact values as {value, exact}; expressions as ucas strings that parse back; unstructured commands give {text}", "type": "object"}, "results": {"description": "every result, when the request ran several commands", "type": "array"}, "notes": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"kind": {"enum": ["rule", "info", "assumed", "default"]}, "text": {"type": "string"}}}}, "conditions": {"description": "where the answer holds", "type": "array", "items": {"type": "string"}}, "checks": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"kind": {"type": "string"}, "points": {"type": "integer"}, "max_diff": {"type": "number"}, "passed": {"type": "boolean"}, "text": {"type": "string"}}}}, "proof": {"type": "object", "properties": {"kind": {"enum": ["symbolic", "exhaustive", "sat", "numeric", "search"]}, "text": {"type": "string"}}}, "files": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"name": {"type": "string"}, "mime": {"type": "string"}, "bytes": {"type": "integer"}, "path": {"type": "string"}, "base64": {"type": "string"}}}}, "text": {"description": "the output as the CLI prints it", "type": "string"}, "error": {"type": "object", "required": ["code", "message"], "properties": {"code": {"enum": ["bad_json", "bad_request", "unknown_command", "parse_error", "domain_error", "unsupported", "failed", "ambiguous", "needs_input", "not_understood", "timeout", "internal"]}, "message": {"type": "string"}, "pos": {"type": "object", "properties": {"line": {"type": "integer"}, "col": {"type": "integer"}}}, "key": {"description": "ambiguous: the args.assume key that picks a reading", "type": "string"}, "readings": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"index": {"type": "integer"}, "reading": {"type": "string"}, "default": {"type": "boolean"}, "how": {"type": "string"}}}}, "how": {"type": "string"}}}}}}, {"name": "complex", "title": "Complex numbers", "description": "Complex numbers and functions: a + bi forms, polar form, real/imaginary parts, trigonometric rewrites (each checked), n-th roots, holomorphy (Cauchy-Riemann), residues, poles.  z and w are complex variables (args.assume.z = \"complex\").\n\nCall with {\"op\": OP, \"args\": {...}}; expressions are ucas syntax strings (x^2 sin(x), isqrt(x: u4)) or an AST ({\"op\": \"+\", \"args\": [...]}).  Ops (* = required arg):\n- complex(f*): as a + bi\n- re(f*): the real part\n- im(f*): the imaginary part\n- conj(f*): the conjugate\n- modulus(f*): the modulus\n- arg(f*): the argument\n- polar(f*): r e^(i theta)\n- trig(f*, mode): equivalent trig forms\n- nthroots(n*, f*): the N complex N-th roots\n- unity(n*): the N-th roots of unity\n- holomorphic(f*): Cauchy-Riemann; the complex derivative\n- residue(f*, at*): the residue at a point\n- poles(f*): the poles and their orders\nEvery op also takes assume (answers to ambiguities, from an error's readings), defaults, timeout_s, files.  Example: {\"op\": \"complex\", \"args\": {\"f\": \"x^3 - 3x\"}}", "inputSchema": {"type": "object", "properties": {"op": {"type": "string", "enum": ["complex", "re", "im", "conj", "modulus", "arg", "polar", "trig", "nthroots", "unity", "holomorphic", "residue", "poles"], "description": "the operation"}, "args": {"type": "object", "description": "the op's named arguments (see the description; the exact schema of each op is in the session tool's schema op)"}}, "required": ["op"], "additionalProperties": false}, "outputSchema": {"type": "object", "required": ["id", "ok", "cmd"], "properties": {"id": {"description": "the request's id, as given (null if none)"}, "ok": {"type": "boolean"}, "cmd": {"type": ["string", "null"]}, "ucas": {"description": "the ucas statements that ran (error positions refer to them)", "type": "string"}, "structured": {"description": "result has fields beyond text", "type": "boolean"}, "result": {"description": "the command's fields (kind, ...); exact values as {value, exact}; expressions as ucas strings that parse back; unstructured commands give {text}", "type": "object"}, "results": {"description": "every result, when the request ran several commands", "type": "array"}, "notes": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"kind": {"enum": ["rule", "info", "assumed", "default"]}, "text": {"type": "string"}}}}, "conditions": {"description": "where the answer holds", "type": "array", "items": {"type": "string"}}, "checks": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"kind": {"type": "string"}, "points": {"type": "integer"}, "max_diff": {"type": "number"}, "passed": {"type": "boolean"}, "text": {"type": "string"}}}}, "proof": {"type": "object", "properties": {"kind": {"enum": ["symbolic", "exhaustive", "sat", "numeric", "search"]}, "text": {"type": "string"}}}, "files": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"name": {"type": "string"}, "mime": {"type": "string"}, "bytes": {"type": "integer"}, "path": {"type": "string"}, "base64": {"type": "string"}}}}, "text": {"description": "the output as the CLI prints it", "type": "string"}, "error": {"type": "object", "required": ["code", "message"], "properties": {"code": {"enum": ["bad_json", "bad_request", "unknown_command", "parse_error", "domain_error", "unsupported", "failed", "ambiguous", "needs_input", "not_understood", "timeout", "internal"]}, "message": {"type": "string"}, "pos": {"type": "object", "properties": {"line": {"type": "integer"}, "col": {"type": "integer"}}}, "key": {"description": "ambiguous: the args.assume key that picks a reading", "type": "string"}, "readings": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"index": {"type": "integer"}, "reading": {"type": "string"}, "default": {"type": "boolean"}, "how": {"type": "string"}}}}, "how": {"type": "string"}}}}}}, {"name": "hypercomplex", "title": "Quaternions and octonions", "description": "Cayley-Dickson algebras (quaternion, octonion, sedenion, cd N): multiplication tables, algebra properties with counterexamples, zero divisors, associators, commutators, 3-D rotations by quaternions, axis-angle, rotation matrices, slerp.\n\nCall with {\"op\": OP, \"args\": {...}}; expressions are ucas syntax strings (x^2 sin(x), isqrt(x: u4)) or an AST ({\"op\": \"+\", \"args\": [...]}).  Ops (* = required arg):\n- multiplication_table(algebra*): an algebra's multiplication table (and the Fano plane)\n- algebra(algebra*, property): an algebra's properties with counterexamples\n- zerodivisors(algebra*): a pair of zero divisors\n- associator(a*, b*, c*): (ab)c - a(bc)\n- commutator(a*, b*): ab - ba\n- rotate(v*, by*, about): rotate a vector by a quaternion or an angle about an axis\n- axisangle(q*): axis and angle to a unit quaternion, or back\n- rotmatrix(q*): a quaternion's 3x3 rotation matrix\n- frommatrix(matrix*): the quaternion of a rotation matrix\n- slerp(q1*, q2*, t*): spherical linear interpolation\nEvery op also takes assume (answers to ambiguities, from an error's readings), defaults, timeout_s, files.  Example: {\"op\": \"multiplication_table\", \"args\": {\"f\": \"x^3 - 3x\"}}", "inputSchema": {"type": "object", "properties": {"op": {"type": "string", "enum": ["multiplication_table", "algebra", "zerodivisors", "associator", "commutator", "rotate", "axisangle", "rotmatrix", "frommatrix", "slerp"], "description": "the operation"}, "args": {"type": "object", "description": "the op's named arguments (see the description; the exact schema of each op is in the session tool's schema op)"}}, "required": ["op"], "additionalProperties": false}, "outputSchema": {"type": "object", "required": ["id", "ok", "cmd"], "properties": {"id": {"description": "the request's id, as given (null if none)"}, "ok": {"type": "boolean"}, "cmd": {"type": ["string", "null"]}, "ucas": {"description": "the ucas statements that ran (error positions refer to them)", "type": "string"}, "structured": {"description": "result has fields beyond text", "type": "boolean"}, "result": {"description": "the command's fields (kind, ...); exact values as {value, exact}; expressions as ucas strings that parse back; unstructured commands give {text}", "type": "object"}, "results": {"description": "every result, when the request ran several commands", "type": "array"}, "notes": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"kind": {"enum": ["rule", "info", "assumed", "default"]}, "text": {"type": "string"}}}}, "conditions": {"description": "where the answer holds", "type": "array", "items": {"type": "string"}}, "checks": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"kind": {"type": "string"}, "points": {"type": "integer"}, "max_diff": {"type": "number"}, "passed": {"type": "boolean"}, "text": {"type": "string"}}}}, "proof": {"type": "object", "properties": {"kind": {"enum": ["symbolic", "exhaustive", "sat", "numeric", "search"]}, "text": {"type": "string"}}}, "files": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"name": {"type": "string"}, "mime": {"type": "string"}, "bytes": {"type": "integer"}, "path": {"type": "string"}, "base64": {"type": "string"}}}}, "text": {"description": "the output as the CLI prints it", "type": "string"}, "error": {"type": "object", "required": ["code", "message"], "properties": {"code": {"enum": ["bad_json", "bad_request", "unknown_command", "parse_error", "domain_error", "unsupported", "failed", "ambiguous", "needs_input", "not_understood", "timeout", "internal"]}, "message": {"type": "string"}, "pos": {"type": "object", "properties": {"line": {"type": "integer"}, "col": {"type": "integer"}}}, "key": {"description": "ambiguous: the args.assume key that picks a reading", "type": "string"}, "readings": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"index": {"type": "integer"}, "reading": {"type": "string"}, "default": {"type": "boolean"}, "how": {"type": "string"}}}}, "how": {"type": "string"}}}}}}, {"name": "rings", "title": "Rings and finite fields", "description": "Number theory and finite fields: Z/n, GF(p^n) (\"ring\": \"GF(2^8)\", \"modulus\": \"aes\"), Z[i]: inverses, orders, phi, factoring, Legendre/Jacobi, square roots mod n, primitive roots, discrete logs, CRT, congruences, division magic numbers, polynomials over GF(q) (factor, irreducible, primitive), matrices mod n, GF(2) bit maps.  A ring argument is \"ring\" and/or \"modulus\" (alone: mod N).\n\nCall with {\"op\": OP, \"args\": {...}}; expressions are ucas syntax strings (x^2 sin(x), isqrt(x: u4)) or an AST ({\"op\": \"+\", \"args\": [...]}).  Ops (* = required arg):\n- ring(ring, modulus, what): a ring's structure (units, zero divisors, ideals ...), an element of it, or a value computed in it\n- inverse_mod(a*, ring, modulus): a multiplicative inverse (of a number, an element, a matrix)\n- order_mod(a*, ring, modulus): multiplicative order (of a residue, an element, a polynomial over GF)\n- phi(n*): Euler's totient\n- carmichael(n*): Carmichael's lambda\n- factorint(n*): integer factorisation (Pollard-Brent, Miller-Rabin)\n- legendre(a*, p*): the Legendre symbol (a/p)\n- jacobi(a*, n*): the Jacobi symbol (a/n)\n- sqrtmod(a*, ring, modulus): square roots mod n (Tonelli-Shanks, Hensel, CRT)\n- qr(n*): the quadratic residues mod n\n- primroot(a, n, ring, modulus): the smallest primitive root mod n, or whether a is one\n- dlog(a*, base, ring, modulus): the discrete logarithm\n- crt(congruences*): the Chinese remainder theorem\n- congruence(equation*, ring, modulus): a linear or polynomial congruence\n- magic(divisor*, type*): the multiply-shift for dividing by a constant\n- ring_factor(p*, ring, modulus): factor a polynomial over a finite field or Z/n (or an element of Z[i])\n- irreducible(p*, ring, modulus): Rabin's irreducibility test\n- primitive(p*, ring, modulus): is the polynomial primitive\n- ring_roots(p*, ring, modulus): roots of a polynomial in Z/n or GF(q)\n- ring_poly(p*, ring, modulus): a polynomial expression reduced over a ring\n- ring_gcd(p*, q*, ring, modulus): polynomial (or Gaussian integer) gcd over a ring\n- ring_norm(a*, ring, modulus): the norm of a quadratic integer\n- matrix(matrix*, op, rhs, ring, modulus): a matrix over Z/n or GF(q): its properties, det, rank, nullspace, inverse, or a solve\n- gf2matrix(f*, type*): a GF(2)-linear bit map as a matrix\nEvery op also takes assume (answers to ambiguities, from an error's readings), defaults, timeout_s, files.  Example: {\"op\": \"ring\", \"args\": {\"f\": \"x^3 - 3x\"}}", "inputSchema": {"type": "object", "properties": {"op": {"type": "string", "enum": ["ring", "inverse_mod", "order_mod", "phi", "carmichael", "factorint", "legendre", "jacobi", "sqrtmod", "qr", "primroot", "dlog", "crt", "congruence", "magic", "ring_factor", "irreducible", "primitive", "ring_roots", "ring_poly", "ring_gcd", "ring_norm", "matrix", "gf2matrix"], "description": "the operation"}, "args": {"type": "object", "description": "the op's named arguments (see the description; the exact schema of each op is in the session tool's schema op)"}}, "required": ["op"], "additionalProperties": false}, "outputSchema": {"type": "object", "required": ["id", "ok", "cmd"], "properties": {"id": {"description": "the request's id, as given (null if none)"}, "ok": {"type": "boolean"}, "cmd": {"type": ["string", "null"]}, "ucas": {"description": "the ucas statements that ran (error positions refer to them)", "type": "string"}, "structured": {"description": "result has fields beyond text", "type": "boolean"}, "result": {"description": "the command's fields (kind, ...); exact values as {value, exact}; expressions as ucas strings that parse back; unstructured commands give {text}", "type": "object"}, "results": {"description": "every result, when the request ran several commands", "type": "array"}, "notes": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"kind": {"enum": ["rule", "info", "assumed", "default"]}, "text": {"type": "string"}}}}, "conditions": {"description": "where the answer holds", "type": "array", "items": {"type": "string"}}, "checks": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"kind": {"type": "string"}, "points": {"type": "integer"}, "max_diff": {"type": "number"}, "passed": {"type": "boolean"}, "text": {"type": "string"}}}}, "proof": {"type": "object", "properties": {"kind": {"enum": ["symbolic", "exhaustive", "sat", "numeric", "search"]}, "text": {"type": "string"}}}, "files": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"name": {"type": "string"}, "mime": {"type": "string"}, "bytes": {"type": "integer"}, "path": {"type": "string"}, "base64": {"type": "string"}}}}, "text": {"description": "the output as the CLI prints it", "type": "string"}, "error": {"type": "object", "required": ["code", "message"], "properties": {"code": {"enum": ["bad_json", "bad_request", "unknown_command", "parse_error", "domain_error", "unsupported", "failed", "ambiguous", "needs_input", "not_understood", "timeout", "internal"]}, "message": {"type": "string"}, "pos": {"type": "object", "properties": {"line": {"type": "integer"}, "col": {"type": "integer"}}}, "key": {"description": "ambiguous: the args.assume key that picks a reading", "type": "string"}, "readings": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"index": {"type": "integer"}, "reading": {"type": "string"}, "default": {"type": "boolean"}, "how": {"type": "string"}}}}, "how": {"type": "string"}}}}}}, {"name": "transforms", "title": "Transforms and series", "description": "Laplace and Z transforms (with the region of convergence) and their inverses, ODEs and recurrences through them, transfer functions, Fourier transforms and series, DFT/DTFT, generating functions, infinite sums and products (test, closed form, numeric value), convergence, radius of convergence, power series, Euler-Maclaurin asymptotics.\n\nCall with {\"op\": OP, \"args\": {...}}; expressions are ucas syntax strings (x^2 sin(x), isqrt(x: u4)) or an AST ({\"op\": \"+\", \"args\": [...]}).  Ops (* = required arg):\n- laplace(f*, var, to_var, period): the one-sided Laplace transform, with its region of convergence\n- ilaplace(f*, var, to_var): the inverse Laplace transform\n- laplace_solve(equations*): a linear ODE with constant coefficients through the Laplace transform\n- ztrans(f*, var, to_var): the one-sided Z transform, with its ROC\n- iztrans(f*, var, to_var): the inverse Z transform (causal)\n- zsolve(equations*): a linear recurrence through the Z transform\n- tf(f*): a transfer function: poles, zeros, stability, impulse response\n- fourier(f*, var, to_var): the Fourier transform\n- ifourier(f*, var, to_var): the inverse Fourier transform\n- fourier_series(f*, var, on, period, terms): a Fourier series\n- dft(values*): the discrete Fourier transform (FFT for powers of two)\n- idft(values*): the inverse DFT\n- dtft(values, f): the discrete-time Fourier transform\n- genfunc(a*, var): the ordinary generating function\n- egf(a*): the exponential generating function\n- infinite_sum(index*, from, f*): an infinite sum: convergence test, closed form, numeric value\n- infinite_product(index*, from, f*): an infinite product\n- converge(a*): convergence tests of sum a_n\n- radius(a*): the radius and interval of convergence of a power series\n- powerseries(f*, var, at): the general term of a power series\n- asymptotic(sum*): Euler-Maclaurin asymptotics of a partial sum\nEvery op also takes assume (answers to ambiguities, from an error's readings), defaults, timeout_s, files.  Example: {\"op\": \"laplace\", \"args\": {\"f\": \"x^3 - 3x\"}}", "inputSchema": {"type": "object", "properties": {"op": {"type": "string", "enum": ["laplace", "ilaplace", "laplace_solve", "ztrans", "iztrans", "zsolve", "tf", "fourier", "ifourier", "fourier_series", "dft", "idft", "dtft", "genfunc", "egf", "infinite_sum", "infinite_product", "converge", "radius", "powerseries", "asymptotic"], "description": "the operation"}, "args": {"type": "object", "description": "the op's named arguments (see the description; the exact schema of each op is in the session tool's schema op)"}}, "required": ["op"], "additionalProperties": false}, "outputSchema": {"type": "object", "required": ["id", "ok", "cmd"], "properties": {"id": {"description": "the request's id, as given (null if none)"}, "ok": {"type": "boolean"}, "cmd": {"type": ["string", "null"]}, "ucas": {"description": "the ucas statements that ran (error positions refer to them)", "type": "string"}, "structured": {"description": "result has fields beyond text", "type": "boolean"}, "result": {"description": "the command's fields (kind, ...); exact values as {value, exact}; expressions as ucas strings that parse back; unstructured commands give {text}", "type": "object"}, "results": {"description": "every result, when the request ran several commands", "type": "array"}, "notes": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"kind": {"enum": ["rule", "info", "assumed", "default"]}, "text": {"type": "string"}}}}, "conditions": {"description": "where the answer holds", "type": "array", "items": {"type": "string"}}, "checks": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"kind": {"type": "string"}, "points": {"type": "integer"}, "max_diff": {"type": "number"}, "passed": {"type": "boolean"}, "text": {"type": "string"}}}}, "proof": {"type": "object", "properties": {"kind": {"enum": ["symbolic", "exhaustive", "sat", "numeric", "search"]}, "text": {"type": "string"}}}, "files": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"name": {"type": "string"}, "mime": {"type": "string"}, "bytes": {"type": "integer"}, "path": {"type": "string"}, "base64": {"type": "string"}}}}, "text": {"description": "the output as the CLI prints it", "type": "string"}, "error": {"type": "object", "required": ["code", "message"], "properties": {"code": {"enum": ["bad_json", "bad_request", "unknown_command", "parse_error", "domain_error", "unsupported", "failed", "ambiguous", "needs_input", "not_understood", "timeout", "internal"]}, "message": {"type": "string"}, "pos": {"type": "object", "properties": {"line": {"type": "integer"}, "col": {"type": "integer"}}}, "key": {"description": "ambiguous: the args.assume key that picks a reading", "type": "string"}, "readings": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"index": {"type": "integer"}, "reading": {"type": "string"}, "default": {"type": "boolean"}, "how": {"type": "string"}}}}, "how": {"type": "string"}}}}}}, {"name": "solids", "title": "Areas and solids of revolution", "description": "Areas under and between curves, solids of revolution (volume by disks/washers/shells, surface area, Pappus), arc length, centroids: exact and numeric values, checks, and a picture.\n\nCall with {\"op\": OP, \"args\": {...}}; expressions are ucas syntax strings (x^2 sin(x), isqrt(x: u4)) or an AST ({\"op\": \"+\", \"args\": [...]}).  Ops (* = required arg):\n- area(f*, from, to, options, nofile): the area under or between curves (exact and numeric; a GIF)\n- revolve(f*, from, to, about, method, options, nofile): the solid of revolution: volume, surface, centroid, Pappus (a GIF)\n- volume(f*, from, to, about, method, nofile): the volume of the solid of revolution\n- surfacearea(f*, from, to, about, nofile): the lateral surface area of the solid\n- arclength(f*, from, to, nofile): the arc length of a curve\n- centroid(f*, from, to, nofile): the centroid of the region under or between curves\nEvery op also takes assume (answers to ambiguities, from an error's readings), defaults, timeout_s, files.  Example: {\"op\": \"area\", \"args\": {\"f\": \"x^3 - 3x\"}}", "inputSchema": {"type": "object", "properties": {"op": {"type": "string", "enum": ["area", "revolve", "volume", "surfacearea", "arclength", "centroid"], "description": "the operation"}, "args": {"type": "object", "description": "the op's named arguments (see the description; the exact schema of each op is in the session tool's schema op)"}}, "required": ["op"], "additionalProperties": false}, "outputSchema": {"type": "object", "required": ["id", "ok", "cmd"], "properties": {"id": {"description": "the request's id, as given (null if none)"}, "ok": {"type": "boolean"}, "cmd": {"type": ["string", "null"]}, "ucas": {"description": "the ucas statements that ran (error positions refer to them)", "type": "string"}, "structured": {"description": "result has fields beyond text", "type": "boolean"}, "result": {"description": "the command's fields (kind, ...); exact values as {value, exact}; expressions as ucas strings that parse back; unstructured commands give {text}", "type": "object"}, "results": {"description": "every result, when the request ran several commands", "type": "array"}, "notes": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"kind": {"enum": ["rule", "info", "assumed", "default"]}, "text": {"type": "string"}}}}, "conditions": {"description": "where the answer holds", "type": "array", "items": {"type": "string"}}, "checks": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"kind": {"type": "string"}, "points": {"type": "integer"}, "max_diff": {"type": "number"}, "passed": {"type": "boolean"}, "text": {"type": "string"}}}}, "proof": {"type": "object", "properties": {"kind": {"enum": ["symbolic", "exhaustive", "sat", "numeric", "search"]}, "text": {"type": "string"}}}, "files": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"name": {"type": "string"}, "mime": {"type": "string"}, "bytes": {"type": "integer"}, "path": {"type": "string"}, "base64": {"type": "string"}}}}, "text": {"description": "the output as the CLI prints it", "type": "string"}, "error": {"type": "object", "required": ["code", "message"], "properties": {"code": {"enum": ["bad_json", "bad_request", "unknown_command", "parse_error", "domain_error", "unsupported", "failed", "ambiguous", "needs_input", "not_understood", "timeout", "internal"]}, "message": {"type": "string"}, "pos": {"type": "object", "properties": {"line": {"type": "integer"}, "col": {"type": "integer"}}}, "key": {"description": "ambiguous: the args.assume key that picks a reading", "type": "string"}, "readings": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"index": {"type": "integer"}, "reading": {"type": "string"}, "default": {"type": "boolean"}, "how": {"type": "string"}}}}, "how": {"type": "string"}}}}}}, {"name": "plot", "title": "Plots and animations", "description": "GIF plots of functions, curves, regions, surfaces, vector and slope fields (bounds chosen from the function's features), and animations of scans and SIMD execution.  The GIF comes back as an image.\n\nCall with {\"op\": OP, \"args\": {...}}; expressions are ucas syntax strings (x^2 sin(x), isqrt(x: u4)) or an AST ({\"op\": \"+\", \"args\": [...]}).  Ops (* = required arg):\n- plot(fs*, options, to, nofile): a GIF plot (files)\n- plot3d(f*, options, to, nofile): a surface (files)\n- neighbourhood(f*, at, nofile): a plot around the interesting part (files)\n- animate(spec, code): an animated GIF: scans, lockstep execution (files)\nEvery op also takes assume (answers to ambiguities, from an error's readings), defaults, timeout_s, files.  Example: {\"op\": \"plot\", \"args\": {\"f\": \"x^3 - 3x\"}}", "inputSchema": {"type": "object", "properties": {"op": {"type": "string", "enum": ["plot", "plot3d", "neighbourhood", "animate"], "description": "the operation"}, "args": {"type": "object", "description": "the op's named arguments (see the description; the exact schema of each op is in the session tool's schema op)"}}, "required": ["op"], "additionalProperties": false}, "outputSchema": {"type": "object", "required": ["id", "ok", "cmd"], "properties": {"id": {"description": "the request's id, as given (null if none)"}, "ok": {"type": "boolean"}, "cmd": {"type": ["string", "null"]}, "ucas": {"description": "the ucas statements that ran (error positions refer to them)", "type": "string"}, "structured": {"description": "result has fields beyond text", "type": "boolean"}, "result": {"description": "the command's fields (kind, ...); exact values as {value, exact}; expressions as ucas strings that parse back; unstructured commands give {text}", "type": "object"}, "results": {"description": "every result, when the request ran several commands", "type": "array"}, "notes": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"kind": {"enum": ["rule", "info", "assumed", "default"]}, "text": {"type": "string"}}}}, "conditions": {"description": "where the answer holds", "type": "array", "items": {"type": "string"}}, "checks": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"kind": {"type": "string"}, "points": {"type": "integer"}, "max_diff": {"type": "number"}, "passed": {"type": "boolean"}, "text": {"type": "string"}}}}, "proof": {"type": "object", "properties": {"kind": {"enum": ["symbolic", "exhaustive", "sat", "numeric", "search"]}, "text": {"type": "string"}}}, "files": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"name": {"type": "string"}, "mime": {"type": "string"}, "bytes": {"type": "integer"}, "path": {"type": "string"}, "base64": {"type": "string"}}}}, "text": {"description": "the output as the CLI prints it", "type": "string"}, "error": {"type": "object", "required": ["code", "message"], "properties": {"code": {"enum": ["bad_json", "bad_request", "unknown_command", "parse_error", "domain_error", "unsupported", "failed", "ambiguous", "needs_input", "not_understood", "timeout", "internal"]}, "message": {"type": "string"}, "pos": {"type": "object", "properties": {"line": {"type": "integer"}, "col": {"type": "integer"}}}, "key": {"description": "ambiguous: the args.assume key that picks a reading", "type": "string"}, "readings": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"index": {"type": "integer"}, "reading": {"type": "string"}, "default": {"type": "boolean"}, "how": {"type": "string"}}}}, "how": {"type": "string"}}}}}}, {"name": "abstract_algebra", "title": "Abstract algebra, exactly", "description": "Exact algebra with certificates: integers of any size (bigint), integer matrices (Smith and Hermite forms with unimodular transforms, kernels, images, solving over Z; rational matrices), finitely generated abelian groups (\"Z/4 + Z/6\", \"coker [[2, 0], [0, 3]]\"): invariants, isomorphisms with explicit maps, Hom, tensor, Tor, Ext, homomorphisms with kernel/image/cokernel, subgroups, element orders, exactness; permutation groups by Schreier-Sims (\"S4\", \"(1 2 3), (1 2)\": order, orbits, solvable, nilpotent, centre, membership, subgroups, cosets, homomorphisms) and Cayley tables; polynomial ideals over Q and F_p (Groebner bases with cofactors, membership certificates, ideal equality); modules over F[x] (Smith form, rational canonical form).  Every claim is checked (U A V = D, preimages, inverse maps) and the check is reported.  For instance {\"op\": \"abiso\", \"args\": {\"g\": \"Z/4 + Z/6\", \"h\": \"Z/2 + Z/12\"}} or {\"op\": \"snf\", \"args\": {\"matrix\": [[2, 4], [6, 8]]}}.\n\nCall with {\"op\": OP, \"args\": {...}}; expressions are ucas syntax strings (x^2 sin(x), isqrt(x: u4)) or an AST ({\"op\": \"+\", \"args\": [...]}).  Ops (* = required arg):\n- bigint(expr*): an exact integer expression of any size (+ - * ^ !, / exact, div floor, % mod, gcd, lcm, abs, isprime, binomial)\n- bigint_factor(n*): prime factorization of an integer of any size (Pollard-Brent rho; product and primality checked)\n- snf(matrix*): Smith normal form U A V = D with U, V and their inverses, verified; the cokernel\n- hnf(matrix*): row Hermite normal form H = U A with U unimodular, verified\n- zmatrix(op, matrix*, rhs): an integer matrix over Z: summary, det, rank, kernel (saturated basis), image (lattice basis), inverse over Z, cokernel group, or solve A x = b over Z\n- qmatrix(op, matrix*, rhs): a matrix over Q (entries like \"1/2\"): rref, det, rank, inverse, nullspace, solve\n- abgroup(group*): a finitely generated abelian group: invariant factors, primary decomposition, order, rank, exponent, torsion, generators\n- abiso(g*, h*): are two abelian groups isomorphic; if so an explicit isomorphism and its inverse, both checked\n- abhom(g*, h*): the group Hom(G, H)\n- abtensor(g*, h*): the tensor product G (x) H\n- abtor(g*, h*): Tor(G, H) from a free resolution\n- abext(g*, h*): Ext(G, H) from a free resolution\n- abmap(from*, to*, matrix*): a homomorphism G -> H given by the images of G's generators (columns, in H's generators): well defined?, kernel, image, cokernel, injective, surjective, inverse\n- abelem(group*, element*): an element of an abelian group: canonical form and order\n- absub(group*, generators*): the subgroup generated by elements, its quotient and index (membership witnesses checked)\n- abexact(g1*, g2*, g3*, f*, g*): is G1 -f-> G2 -g-> G3 exact at G2 (with preimages of ker g as the certificate)\n- permgroup(group*): a permutation group by Schreier-Sims: order (exact, any size), base and strong generators, orbits, abelian, derived and lower central series, solvable, nilpotent, centre\n- permelem(group*, perm*): is a permutation in the group (sifting, with the word in the transversals as the certificate); its order\n- permsub(h*, g*): H in G: subgroup?, normal?, index, normal closure, coset representatives\n- permhom(from*, to*, images*): does sending G's generators to the given permutations define a homomorphism G -> H\n- cayley(table*): a finite group by its Cayley table (entries 0..n-1): the axioms checked, abelian, element orders, solvable, nilpotent\n- groebner(polys*, order, modulus, vars): the reduced Groebner basis of an ideal of polynomials over Q or F_p, each element with its cofactors in the generators (Buchberger with criteria; verified)\n- idealmember(h*, polys*, order, modulus, vars): is h in the ideal: the cofactors h = sum c_j f_j (multiplied out and checked), or the nonzero normal form\n- idealeq(i*, j*, order, modulus, vars): compare two ideals: equal, one inside the other, or neither (each inclusion certified by cofactors)\n- fxmodule(matrix*, modulus): F^n as an F[x]-module with x acting by a matrix: invariant factors, minimal and characteristic polynomial, rational canonical form (Smith form over F[x])\n- pmsnf(matrix*, modulus): the Smith normal form of a matrix of polynomials in one variable over Q or F_p, with U and V\nEvery op also takes assume (answers to ambiguities, from an error's readings), defaults, timeout_s, files.  Example: {\"op\": \"bigint\", \"args\": {\"f\": \"x^3 - 3x\"}}", "inputSchema": {"type": "object", "properties": {"op": {"type": "string", "enum": ["bigint", "bigint_factor", "snf", "hnf", "zmatrix", "qmatrix", "abgroup", "abiso", "abhom", "abtensor", "abtor", "abext", "abmap", "abelem", "absub", "abexact", "permgroup", "permelem", "permsub", "permhom", "cayley", "groebner", "idealmember", "idealeq", "fxmodule", "pmsnf"], "description": "the operation"}, "args": {"type": "object", "description": "the op's named arguments (see the description; the exact schema of each op is in the session tool's schema op)"}}, "required": ["op"], "additionalProperties": false}, "outputSchema": {"type": "object", "required": ["id", "ok", "cmd"], "properties": {"id": {"description": "the request's id, as given (null if none)"}, "ok": {"type": "boolean"}, "cmd": {"type": ["string", "null"]}, "ucas": {"description": "the ucas statements that ran (error positions refer to them)", "type": "string"}, "structured": {"description": "result has fields beyond text", "type": "boolean"}, "result": {"description": "the command's fields (kind, ...); exact values as {value, exact}; expressions as ucas strings that parse back; unstructured commands give {text}", "type": "object"}, "results": {"description": "every result, when the request ran several commands", "type": "array"}, "notes": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"kind": {"enum": ["rule", "info", "assumed", "default"]}, "text": {"type": "string"}}}}, "conditions": {"description": "where the answer holds", "type": "array", "items": {"type": "string"}}, "checks": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"kind": {"type": "string"}, "points": {"type": "integer"}, "max_diff": {"type": "number"}, "passed": {"type": "boolean"}, "text": {"type": "string"}}}}, "proof": {"type": "object", "properties": {"kind": {"enum": ["symbolic", "exhaustive", "sat", "numeric", "search"]}, "text": {"type": "string"}}}, "files": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"name": {"type": "string"}, "mime": {"type": "string"}, "bytes": {"type": "integer"}, "path": {"type": "string"}, "base64": {"type": "string"}}}}, "text": {"description": "the output as the CLI prints it", "type": "string"}, "error": {"type": "object", "required": ["code", "message"], "properties": {"code": {"enum": ["bad_json", "bad_request", "unknown_command", "parse_error", "domain_error", "unsupported", "failed", "ambiguous", "needs_input", "not_understood", "timeout", "internal"]}, "message": {"type": "string"}, "pos": {"type": "object", "properties": {"line": {"type": "integer"}, "col": {"type": "integer"}}}, "key": {"description": "ambiguous: the args.assume key that picks a reading", "type": "string"}, "readings": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"index": {"type": "integer"}, "reading": {"type": "string"}, "default": {"type": "boolean"}, "how": {"type": "string"}}}}, "how": {"type": "string"}}}}}}, {"name": "session", "title": "Session", "description": "The session: define a function (typed parameters), list the state, keep answers to ambiguities (assume), reset, the interface schema, the cost models.\n\nCall with {\"op\": OP, \"args\": {...}}; expressions are ucas syntax strings (x^2 sin(x), isqrt(x: u4)) or an AST ({\"op\": \"+\", \"args\": [...]}).  Ops (* = required arg):\n- define(name*, params, body*, where): define a function: name(params) = body [where ...]; every parameter needs a type (or a range)\n- state(): the session: functions, models, bases, assumptions\n- assume(set, clear): session-wide answers to ambiguities (merged under each request's args.assume)\n- reset(): drop every definition (the process image is restarted)\n- schema(): this interface as JSON Schema\n- funcs(): every defined function\n- models(): the cost models\n- use(model*): make a cost model active\n- help(): the command summary\nEvery op also takes assume (answers to ambiguities, from an error's readings), defaults, timeout_s, files.  Example: {\"op\": \"define\", \"args\": {\"f\": \"x^3 - 3x\"}}", "inputSchema": {"type": "object", "properties": {"op": {"type": "string", "enum": ["define", "state", "assume", "reset", "schema", "funcs", "models", "use", "help"], "description": "the operation"}, "args": {"type": "object", "description": "the op's named arguments (see the description; the exact schema of each op is in the session tool's schema op)"}}, "required": ["op"], "additionalProperties": false}, "outputSchema": {"type": "object", "required": ["id", "ok", "cmd"], "properties": {"id": {"description": "the request's id, as given (null if none)"}, "ok": {"type": "boolean"}, "cmd": {"type": ["string", "null"]}, "ucas": {"description": "the ucas statements that ran (error positions refer to them)", "type": "string"}, "structured": {"description": "result has fields beyond text", "type": "boolean"}, "result": {"description": "the command's fields (kind, ...); exact values as {value, exact}; expressions as ucas strings that parse back; unstructured commands give {text}", "type": "object"}, "results": {"description": "every result, when the request ran several commands", "type": "array"}, "notes": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"kind": {"enum": ["rule", "info", "assumed", "default"]}, "text": {"type": "string"}}}}, "conditions": {"description": "where the answer holds", "type": "array", "items": {"type": "string"}}, "checks": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"kind": {"type": "string"}, "points": {"type": "integer"}, "max_diff": {"type": "number"}, "passed": {"type": "boolean"}, "text": {"type": "string"}}}}, "proof": {"type": "object", "properties": {"kind": {"enum": ["symbolic", "exhaustive", "sat", "numeric", "search"]}, "text": {"type": "string"}}}, "files": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"name": {"type": "string"}, "mime": {"type": "string"}, "bytes": {"type": "integer"}, "path": {"type": "string"}, "base64": {"type": "string"}}}}, "text": {"description": "the output as the CLI prints it", "type": "string"}, "error": {"type": "object", "required": ["code", "message"], "properties": {"code": {"enum": ["bad_json", "bad_request", "unknown_command", "parse_error", "domain_error", "unsupported", "failed", "ambiguous", "needs_input", "not_understood", "timeout", "internal"]}, "message": {"type": "string"}, "pos": {"type": "object", "properties": {"line": {"type": "integer"}, "col": {"type": "integer"}}}, "key": {"description": "ambiguous: the args.assume key that picks a reading", "type": "string"}, "readings": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"index": {"type": "integer"}, "reading": {"type": "string"}, "default": {"type": "boolean"}, "how": {"type": "string"}}}}, "how": {"type": "string"}}}}}}, {"name": "homological", "title": "Homological algebra", "description": "Exact homology and cohomology of spaces (spheres, tori, RP^n, CP^n, Klein bottle, lens spaces L(m,q), products, wedges, suspensions, simplicial or cellular complexes you give) with any f.g. abelian coefficients; long exact sequences with the snake lemma; the Bockstein spectral sequence (pages, d_r, E_inf), element tracing, and the check of bockstein.pdf's Proposition 0.1.  Every claim carries its checks (d o d = 0, exactness, well-defined induced maps, universal coefficients).\n\nCall with {\"op\": OP, \"args\": {...}}; expressions are ucas syntax strings (x^2 sin(x), isqrt(x: u4)) or an AST ({\"op\": \"+\", \"args\": [...]}).  Ops (* = required arg):\n- space(space*, unreduced): a cell complex: its cells, Euler characteristic and boundaries (d o d = 0 checked)\n- homology(space*, unreduced, coefficients, generators): H_n(X; G) for every n, exactly, with the universal coefficient theorem as a check\n- cohomology(space*, unreduced, coefficients, generators): H^n(X; G) for every n, exactly, with both universal coefficient theorems as checks\n- les(space*, unreduced, modulus*): the long exact sequence of 0 -> C -m-> C -> C (x) Z/m -> 0 on cochains, the connecting map by the snake lemma, exactness verified at every spot\n- bockstein(space*, unreduced, p*, pages): the Bockstein spectral sequence: pages E_r, D_r and d_r of the exact couple of 0 -> C -p-> C -> C (x) Z/p -> 0, derived exactly until stable\n- bockstein_trace(space*, unreduced, p*, degree*, element, page): trace a in H^n(X; Z) through the Bockstein spectral sequence: j_r(p^(r-1) a) in E_r, in ker d_r?, in im d_r? (with a preimage)\n- prop01(space*, unreduced, p*, pages): check Proposition 0.1 of bockstein.pdf on a space: for a generating a Z summand of H^n(X; Z), j_r(p^(r-1) a) is in ker d_r and not in im d_r, for every n and every r (all r up to the stable page, which covers the rest)\nEvery op also takes assume (answers to ambiguities, from an error's readings), defaults, timeout_s, files.  Example: {\"op\": \"space\", \"args\": {\"f\": \"x^3 - 3x\"}}", "inputSchema": {"type": "object", "properties": {"op": {"type": "string", "enum": ["space", "homology", "cohomology", "les", "bockstein", "bockstein_trace", "prop01"], "description": "the operation"}, "args": {"type": "object", "description": "the op's named arguments (see the description; the exact schema of each op is in the session tool's schema op)"}}, "required": ["op"], "additionalProperties": false}, "outputSchema": {"type": "object", "required": ["id", "ok", "cmd"], "properties": {"id": {"description": "the request's id, as given (null if none)"}, "ok": {"type": "boolean"}, "cmd": {"type": ["string", "null"]}, "ucas": {"description": "the ucas statements that ran (error positions refer to them)", "type": "string"}, "structured": {"description": "result has fields beyond text", "type": "boolean"}, "result": {"description": "the command's fields (kind, ...); exact values as {value, exact}; expressions as ucas strings that parse back; unstructured commands give {text}", "type": "object"}, "results": {"description": "every result, when the request ran several commands", "type": "array"}, "notes": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"kind": {"enum": ["rule", "info", "assumed", "default"]}, "text": {"type": "string"}}}}, "conditions": {"description": "where the answer holds", "type": "array", "items": {"type": "string"}}, "checks": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"kind": {"type": "string"}, "points": {"type": "integer"}, "max_diff": {"type": "number"}, "passed": {"type": "boolean"}, "text": {"type": "string"}}}}, "proof": {"type": "object", "properties": {"kind": {"enum": ["symbolic", "exhaustive", "sat", "numeric", "search"]}, "text": {"type": "string"}}}, "files": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"name": {"type": "string"}, "mime": {"type": "string"}, "bytes": {"type": "integer"}, "path": {"type": "string"}, "base64": {"type": "string"}}}}, "text": {"description": "the output as the CLI prints it", "type": "string"}, "error": {"type": "object", "required": ["code", "message"], "properties": {"code": {"enum": ["bad_json", "bad_request", "unknown_command", "parse_error", "domain_error", "unsupported", "failed", "ambiguous", "needs_input", "not_understood", "timeout", "internal"]}, "message": {"type": "string"}, "pos": {"type": "object", "properties": {"line": {"type": "integer"}, "col": {"type": "integer"}}}, "key": {"description": "ambiguous: the args.assume key that picks a reading", "type": "string"}, "readings": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"index": {"type": "integer"}, "reading": {"type": "string"}, "default": {"type": "boolean"}, "how": {"type": "string"}}}}, "how": {"type": "string"}}}}}}, {"name": "ucas", "description": "raw ucas statements (the escape hatch).  Any ucas statements, as typed at the ucas> prompt, e.g. \"f(x: u8) = x*x\\nrange f\" or \"x[0] = 1; x[k+1] = 2x[k]\"", "inputSchema": {"type": "object", "properties": {"source": {"type": "string", "description": "ucas source; several lines allowed"}, "code": {"type": "string", "description": "a code block for the statement (SPIR-V assembly or GLSL)"}, "assume": {"type": "object", "description": "answers to ambiguities: {key: reading or index}, e.g. {\"caret\": \"power\", \"z\": \"complex\"}"}, "defaults": {"type": "boolean", "description": "take the default reading of every ambiguity (as the CLI does with a note) instead of an error"}, "timeout_s": {"$ref": "#/$defs/number", "description": "wall-clock limit; the request runs in a forked child and the state is unchanged on a timeout"}, "files": {"enum": ["write", "base64", "both", "none"], "description": "what to do with files: write (to --dir, default), base64 (inline, nothing written), both, none"}, "answers": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "string"}, "description": "replies to follow-up questions, in order"}}, "required": ["source"], "additionalProperties": false, "$defs": {"number": {"description": "a JSON number, or a constant expression in ucas syntax (\"pi/2\", \"inf\")", "type": ["number", "string"]}}}, "outputSchema": {"type": "object", "required": ["id", "ok", "cmd"], "properties": {"id": {"description": "the request's id, as given (null if none)"}, "ok": {"type": "boolean"}, "cmd": {"type": ["string", "null"]}, "ucas": {"description": "the ucas statements that ran (error positions refer to them)", "type": "string"}, "structured": {"description": "result has fields beyond text", "type": "boolean"}, "result": {"description": "the command's fields (kind, ...); exact values as {value, exact}; expressions as ucas strings that parse back; unstructured commands give {text}", "type": "object"}, "results": {"description": "every result, when the request ran several commands", "type": "array"}, "notes": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"kind": {"enum": ["rule", "info", "assumed", "default"]}, "text": {"type": "stri